-- title:
--   Pull-back of a presentation along a C-algebra map
-- statement:
--   The statement is set in the full Čerednik–Drinfeld frame for fake elliptic curves; all of the frame is carried as hypotheses, and the assertion itself concerns only the functoriality of the point map `ptR` of a representing functor `PR` over a base ring $C$.
--
--   **Arithmetic data.** Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$, and a nonzero squarefree $N$ with $r \nmid N$ and $\bar r \nmid N$ (`hrr`, `hrN`, `hrbarN`, `hN`). A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), an irreducible $\pi \in \mathcal O$, completeness of $\mathcal O$ for the ideal $(\pi)$ (`hcomplete`), residue cardinality $\#(\mathcal O/\pi) = r$ (`hres`), and $(r) = (\pi)$ in $\mathcal O$ (`hunr`); $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal O$. An $\mathcal O$-algebra $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$, a characteristic-zero domain, with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), that ideal being maximal (`hOnr_max`), every element of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfying a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial of positive degree over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ having a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ (`hFr`). A homomorphism $\mathrm{vdet} : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ which, by `hvdet`, computes the $\pi$-adic valuation of the determinant: $\mathrm{vdet}(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ for some $u \in \mathcal O^{\times}$.
--
--   **Quaternionic data.** Rationals $a, b$ with `hB`, which says that $a > 0$ or $b > 0$ and that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a, b] \otimes \mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly at the places $v$ above $r$ and $\bar r$; $\Lambda$ a maximal order (an order, i.e. containing $1$, multiplicatively closed, spanning over $\mathbb Q$ and finitely generated, and maximal among such), with `hΛℤ` asserting that all rational integers lie in $\Lambda$, and `coord` a pair-of-Witt-vector coordinate system on $\Lambda$ satisfying `IsOrderCoord` (additivity, normalisation at $1$, the Frobenius-twisted multiplication rule, injectivity, $r$-adic density and the trace identity). On the definite side, rationals $a_1, b_1$ with `hdef` ($a_1 < 0$, $b_1 < 0$, and division exactly at $\bar r$), a maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ (an intersection of two maximal orders of relative index $N$) with $R_1 \le \Lambda_1$, an adelic unit $n_1$ in `primeHeckeSet R₁ r` such that `meetOrder R₁ n₁` is Eichler of level $N r$ (`hS₁`), an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0$ into $M_2(K_0)$, and the place $v$ of $\mathbb Q$ above $r$. The group $\Gamma_t$ is, elementwise, the group of units integral away from $v$ (`hΓt`); `s`, `sf`, `hs` provide for each prime $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$ an element $s_\ell$ of reduced norm $\ell$ together with an adelic unit $sf_\ell$ agreeing with $s_\ell$ away from $r$, trivial at $r$, and such that the diagonal $\ell$ times $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` when $\ell \mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` otherwise; $\Gamma_{t,\ell} = \Gamma_t \cap s_\ell \Gamma_t s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`); and $\bar w$ is a unit of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma_t$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   **Moduli frame.** A scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point map `pt` and `h𝒳 : IsCoarseModuli` (isomorphism invariance, compatibility with pull-backs, bijectivity on geometric points over algebraically closed fields, and the universal property). A full level $n \ge 3$ with $r \nmid n$, $\bar r \nmid n$ and $\gcd(n,N) = 1$, a fine moduli scheme $M$ with point map `ptF` and `hM : IsFineModuli` (isomorphism invariance, pull-back compatibility, and bijectivity of `ptF` over every ring), together with a group $G$ acting by $\rho : G \to \operatorname{Aut} M$ with labels $\chi : G \to \Lambda$ and `hρ : IsLevelTwistAction` (the action is over the base, realises the level twists, and the labelling is multiplicative, surjective and injective modulo $n$). A forgetful morphism $p : M \to \mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ (`hp`), invariant under $G$ (`hρp`), and compatible with the point maps (`hp_pt`). Hecke data: schemes $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ for primes $\ell \notin\{r,\bar r\}$ with point maps `ptT` on curves with extra level $\ell$ and the coarse moduli property `h𝒴`, degeneracy morphisms $d_0, d_1 : \mathcal Y_\ell \to \mathcal X$ over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) described on points by `hd₀` (forget the extra level) and `hd₁` (pass to the quotient by a level isogeny); and Atkin–Lehner morphisms $a_r, a_{\bar r} : \mathcal X \to \mathcal X$ over the base with the moduli descriptions `har`, `harbar` in terms of `IsAtkinLehnerQuotient`.
--
--   **Special-fibre data.** A fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ over that ring (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of dimension $2$ along the unit section of $A_0$, and `hA₀`, which says that $\theta_0$ are formal coordinates for the group law of $A_0$ and that the $\Lambda$-action is given through `coord` by the series of $X_0$. Endomorphisms $e, e'$ of $A_0$ indexed by $\Gamma_t$, over the base (`he`), with degrees `deg`, subject to `hE1` (each pair $(e_\gamma, e'_\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg \gamma}$ preserving the level structure), `hE1mul` (multiplicativity up to multiplication by powers of $r$), `hE1sc` and `hE1'` (scalars in $\Gamma_t$ act by integer multiplication up to powers of $r$, and conversely), `hE2` (compatibility of each $e_\gamma$ with the formal module: for every injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $X_0$-action and $\varpi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is a single $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $e_\gamma$ is induced on $\theta_0$ by an element $\varepsilon$ of that centraliser with $E_0\varepsilon = r^{k_\gamma}\, g\, \iota_0(\gamma)\, g^{-1}$), `hE3` (for each full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$ a labelling $\mathrm{lab} : \Gamma_t \to \Lambda$ computing the action of $e_\gamma$ on it, multiplicative and scalar-compatible modulo $n$), and `hE4` (over an algebraically closed field, every $r$-power isogeny preserving the level on a pull-back of $A_0$ comes from some $e_\gamma$ up to powers of $r$). Further, an order $R_2 \le R_1$ with $r$-power denominators (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`, `hR₂r`), endomorphisms $\hat e$ of $A_0$ indexed by $R_2$ over the base (`hê`), and the clauses `hE5a` (each $\hat e_x$ respects the group law, commutes with the $\Lambda$-action and preserves level), `hE5b1`–`hE5b3` (unitality, multiplicativity, and integers acting through $\Lambda$), `hE5c` ($\hat e_{\bar x}$ composed with $\hat e_x$ is multiplication by $\mathrm{nrd}\,x$), `hE5d` (agreement of $\hat e$ with $e$ up to powers of $r$ when $x = r^{k}\gamma$) and `hE5e` (a single $g$ serving both the $\Gamma_t$- and the $R_2$-compatibilities). A second Atkin–Lehner package on the special fibre: $A_{0w}$, morphisms $a_w, a_w', b_w, b_w'$ with the stated compatibilities over the base, `hALw` (an Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ via $a_w, a_w'$), `hBSw` (an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$), `hBSwlev` (level preservation) and `hJOINTw` (the formal compatibility of `hE2` extended to $a_w$ followed by $b_w$, matched with $\iota_0(\bar w)$). A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$.
--
--   **Drinfeld side.** A ring map $\iota : \mathbb{W}(\mathbb F_{r^2}) \to O^{\mathrm{nr}}$, a special formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ of height $4$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ (`hΦ`, `hΦ4`), a moduli package $MD$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`), a map $\eta$ from rigidified $\Phi$-objects to $MD$-points with `hη` in three clauses (on admissible rigidifications $\eta$ identifies exactly isomorphic objects; $\eta$ commutes with base change; every $MD$-point is, on a finite cover of the base by principal opens, in the image of $\eta$ on an admissible object), and an injective map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action and $\varpi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image is, after scaling by $r^{m}$, exactly the matrices over $\mathcal O$ (`hE₀`). The Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison is encoded by $eD$, a map from the $G$-points of $MD$ over a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent to pairs consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$ and a Deligne datum, subject to `hnatD` (naturality), `hbijD` (bijectivity), `hfstD` (the first component is the dictionary leg), `hGLD` (the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action corresponds to `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct`, i.e. the leg is twisted by $\mathrm{Fr}^{-\mathrm{vdet}(g)}$ and the datum is pulled back along $g^{-1}$), `hPiD` and `hPiexD` ($\pi$-translates exist and correspond to a single Frobenius twist of the leg with the datum unchanged). Also a map $\kappa : O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi) \to O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ compatible with the quotient maps (`hκ`), and an isogeny $\beta_0$ from $\Phi$ to $X_0$ transported along $\kappa$, of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`).
--
--   **The dictionary $\Xi$.** A map $\Xi$ assigning to a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$ and a rigidified fake elliptic curve over $B$ a $G$-point of $MD$, with `hΞleg` (over connected $B$ the leg of $\Xi$ is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$), `hΞnat` (naturality under pull-back of curve and rigidification), `hΞiso` (invariance under isomorphisms of curves admitting the displayed comparison of rigidifications up to $r$-power multiplications) and `hΞdef` (for connected $B$ with $r$ nilpotent and a formal-module structure on the curve, there are $j \le 1$ and an admissible rigidified $\Phi$-object $t$ transported from $\theta_0$, $\kappa$, $\beta_0$ with $\Xi$ given by $\eta$ applied to $t$ over the leg twisted by $\mathrm{Fr}^{-j}$). Finally $g_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ with `heqΓ` and `heqW`: translating a rigidification by $e_\gamma$, respectively passing to an Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ with the displayed comparison, corresponds under $\Xi$ to the action of $r^{c} g_0 \iota_0(\gamma) g_0^{-1}$, respectively $r^{c} g_0 \iota_0(\bar w) g_0^{-1}$, for some $c \in \mathbb Z$.
--
--   **The representing functor.** $C$ is a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra in which $\pi$ is nilpotent (`hCπ`), with an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\chi_C : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to C$; $PR$ is a functor on $C$-algebras; and `ptR` assigns, to a $C$-algebra $S$ carrying a compatible $\mathcal O$-structure, a leg $\psi_S : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to S$ factoring as $\chi_C$ followed by $C \to S$, a fake elliptic curve with full level $n$ over $S$ and a rigidification of it relative to $\psi_S$, an element of $PR(S)$. The laws are: `hR2` (naturality of `ptR` along a $C$-algebra map $\varphi$ whenever the curves-with-level are pull-backs via a comparison $g$ carrying the level point, and the rigidifications are pull-backs along $\varphi$ via $g$), `hR3s` (`ptR` is surjective on $PR(S)$), `hR3i` (over connected $S$, equality of two values of `ptR` yields an isomorphism of curves-with-level together with the displayed comparison of rigidifications up to $r$-power multiplications) and `hR1` (the converse: such an isomorphism and comparison force equality of the two values of `ptR`).
--
--   **Input and conclusion.** Let $S$ and $S'$ be Noetherian $C$-algebras with compatible $\mathcal O$-structures, $\varphi : S \to S'$ a $C$-algebra map, $\pi$ nilpotent in $S$ (`hS`), $\psi_S$ a leg factoring through $\chi_C$ (`hψS`), $u$ a fake elliptic curve over $S$ with full level-$n$ structure, $\rho$ a rigidification of its curve relative to $\psi_S$, `hmod` an element of $\Lambda$, and $P'$ a full level-$n$ structure on the curve of $u$ whose point is the push-forward of the tautological level point $u_2.P$ under the action of `hmod` (`hP'`).
--
--   Then there exist: a proof that $\pi$ is nilpotent in $S'$; a proof that the restriction of $\varphi$ to $\mathcal O$-algebras composed with $\psi_S$ is the structure map $C \to S'$ composed with $\chi_C$; a fake elliptic curve with full level $n$, $u'$, over $S'$; a rigidification $\rho'$ of its curve relative to that composite leg; a morphism $g_E$ from the curve of $u'$ to the curve of $u$ exhibiting the former as the pull-back of the latter along $\varphi$ in the sense of `FakeEllipticCurve.IsPullbackVia` (a Cartesian square over $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi$, compatibility with the group laws and the $\Lambda$-action, and the level subscheme condition); a proof that the tautological level point of $u'$ followed by $g_E$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi$ followed by the tautological level point of $u$; a proof that $\rho'$ is the pull-back of $\rho$ along $\varphi$ via $g_E$; and a full level-$n$ structure $P''$ on the curve of $u'$ such that its point followed by $g_E$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi$ followed by the point of $P'$, and such that the point of $P''$ is the push-forward of the tautological level point of $u'$ under the action of the same element `hmod`; and for these data the two equalities in $PR(S')$ hold:
--   $$\mathrm{ptR}_{S'}(u', \rho') = PR(\varphi)\bigl(\mathrm{ptR}_{S}(u, \rho)\bigr), \qquad \mathrm{ptR}_{S'}\bigl((u'_1, P''), \rho'\bigr) = PR(\varphi)\bigl(\mathrm{ptR}_{S}((u_1, P'), \rho)\bigr).$$
--
--   This is the base-change step for presentations of points of the representing functor $PR$ of rigidified fake elliptic curves with full level $n$ in the Čerednik–Drinfeld frame: a curve with level, its rigidification, and a level point twisted by an element of $\Lambda$ are all pulled back simultaneously along a map of Noetherian $C$-algebras, and the two resulting values of `ptR` are identified with the images under $PR(\varphi)$. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.exists_label_natural_iff_exists_ptR_eq_of_rigidifiedToG_connInj_pr`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.exists_label_natural_iff_exists_ptR_eq_of_rigidifiedToG_connInj_pr), where the naturality of the labelling of presentations is established.
